    da_virtual_bids: { cell: "K", ev: "pjm-frontier-path §2; pjm-157 (results/calibration/FINDING-pjm157-cc-object-does-not-survive-phase0-2026-08-05.md §1.1 — OPEN QUESTION on the armed keeper, status UNCHANGED because nothing was adjudicated: no A/B, no LP; probe _pjm157_virtual_channel.py); pjm-158 (results/calibration/FINDING-pjm158-da-virtual-clearing-2026-08-06.md §2-§5 + PREREG-pjm158-da-virtual-clearing-2026-08-05.md; runs 2026-08-06-pjm-158-control-virtual + 2026-08-06-pjm-158-novirtual-disarmed; probes _pjm158_virtual_gain.py, _pjm158_virtual_basis.py, _pjm158_virtual_shape.py, _pjm158_coal_basis.py) — PHASE-0 MEASURED, on the measured 2023-2025 hrl_da_incs_decs corpus. THREE results. (1) The N_RUNGS compression is EXACT, so the hoped-for representation-exact fix does NOT exist: it contributes −0.068/−0.008/−0.110 TWh, λ0 displacement −0.19/−0.23/−0.48 $/MWh, and 8→64 rungs moves cleared volume ≤0.13 TWh; a five-step attribution chain (anchor → price level → zonal dispersion → ladder → the LP) reproduces the LP's own cleared volume to ≤0.09 TWh and puts 97-99 % of the deviation on the PRICE the curve is cleared at. (2) The measured gain is dNet/dλ = −440/−463/−340 MW per $/MWh (steepest overnight h00-h09, flattest at the afternoon peak), i.e. 3.0-4.1 TWh/yr per uniform $1/MWh — C1 is quantitatively conditional on C3b. (3) THE STRUCTURAL DEFECT — the mechanism's rule-13 anchor REPRODUCES at actual DA prices (−0.755/−1.620/+0.204 TWh, pjm-105's −0.68/−0.95/+1.32 to within rung discretization) but the model's dual is gated as REAL-TIME by the scorer's own definition (calibration_verdict.score_price_mean: 'vs actual RT (fallback DA) … perfect-foresight dispatch LP prices RT physics, not day-ahead risk', DA a non-gated diagnostic; PJM's bench carries rt_lw in all three years so the RT branch is taken). Clearing the SAME curve at actual RT gives +5.082/+3.001/+6.781 TWh of phantom DEMAND, so the DA−RT basis alone is +5.836/+4.621/+6.577 TWh — split LEVEL +2.991/+0.973/+2.432 and SHAPE/dispersion +2.845/+3.648/+4.145, neither closable alone. A model that hit its own load-bearing price gate EXACTLY would still miss the invariant by +3 to +7 TWh, so the deviation is NOT a C3b symptom a better price would cure. Note the mirror-image: pjm-102 was condemned for one-sided phantom DEMAND (+10.3/+14.8/+17.2), while the adopted symmetric form clears at up to 7.45 TWh of phantom SUPPLY — and pjm-105's own table records it moving 2024 CC_REGULAR +9.07 → −1.78. Hour-of-day reshaping DOES survive in the LP (corr +0.755/+0.661/+0.651 vs the reference position) but runs 1.3-1.4× too large, concentrated in h00-h05. PHASE-1 A/B SOLVED AND BOTH ARMS REGISTERED: 2026-08-06-pjm-158-control-virtual (armed) vs 2026-08-06-pjm-158-novirtual-disarmed (single delta pjm_da_virtual_bids=false), 2023-2025 each in one invocation. The CONTROL reproduces the pjm-152 keeper BYTE-IDENTICALLY (max |Δ| 0.00000 TWh over every class and year), so HEAD is solve-identical for PJM's backcast path and the delta is clean. ALL THREE PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTIONS CONFIRMED: P1 disarming moves NG-equivalent error −9.94/−9.25/+1.72 → −3.99/−4.07/−0.29 (toward zero in all three years, the pre-registered seam caveat firing at +1.00/+0.67/+0.37 TWh into the unconstrained star node); P2 CC_REGULAR moves +5.220/+6.848/+2.689 TWh, far above the 2 TWh falsification bar, so the cleared virtual IS displacing CC_REGULAR and pjm-157 §1.1's channel is confirmed; P3 C3a error and hourly MAE degrade in all three years (9.20→9.94, 10.50→11.82, 13.97→15.24 $/MWh). RUBRIC: control passes EVERY criterion; treatment FAILS C3c-2025 (22h >$200 vs RT actual 59h, 0.37×) — exactly the criterion pjm-105's adoption note credited the layer with fixing. CELL STAYS K, DEPARTING FROM THE PREREG's OWN K→R RECOMMENDATION WITH CAUSE (finding §5.5): that rule assumed disarming would IMPROVE the fit, making R the rule-1-clean call; the measured outcome is the opposite on every load-bearing and supporting gate, and rejecting real market structure violates rule 1 as firmly as keeping a fitted one. The defect is rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] shaped — a real measured input MISALIGNED TO OUR REPRESENTATION — so it is documented, not buried: the layer's cleared volume must NOT be read as a measured cleared volume, and the root cause (the LP carries ONE price series, gated as RT, while the curve needs a DA price) is an ARCHITECTURE question inside PJM's owner-declared-closed price-formation frontier (pjm-142), ESCALATED TO THE OWNER rather than pulled as a lever. STANDING WARNING for the PJM price lane: the basis (+5.8/+4.6/+6.6) and the model's price error (−12.5/−9.6/−5.9) currently OPPOSE each other by coincidence, so improving C3b toward RT GROWS this layer's phantom energy toward +5 to +7 TWh of phantom DEMAND — toward the condemned pjm-102 clamp, not away from it. Also recorded: classFull vs the CEMS census differ by a stable +6-7 TWh for CC_REGULAR in every year, so the 2022 CC_REGULAR error is +18.28 TWh on the gate's own basis, not +25.40 (the same three-bases trap Question C resolves for coal; the CC object itself was NOT re-tested). CELL UNCHANGED AT K, RE-MEASURED NOT RE-OPENED — pjm-166 (2026-09-06, results/calibration/FINDING-pjm166-c1-object-phase0-2026-09-06.md §3; zero LP, committed sidecars only, NO A/B, no mechanism armed): pjm-158 measured this defect on 2023-2025 ONLY. The two held-out rungs put the layer on the OTHER SIDE of its crossing price. Net cleared virtual position (VIRTUAL_INC + VIRTUAL_DEC, TWh): 2021 -6.14, 2022 -9.91, 2023 +7.40, 2024 +6.48, 2025 -0.89 — i.e. 6 to 10 TWh of net phantom DEMAND out of sample against up to 7.45 TWh of phantom SUPPLY in sample, against the mechanism's own rule-13 anchor of ~0 at actual DA prices. THIS IS THE pjm-158 STANDING WARNING REALIZED: the phantom energy has moved toward the condemned pjm-102 clamp direction, it is ~2x larger out of sample, and the two years it fails on are exactly the two years C1 fails. Sign of the net virtual position agrees with the sign of the total-fossil surplus in 5 of 5 years (surplus +19.6/+26.7/-3.7/-7.9/+13.5 TWh, classFull basis, against model demand right to +/-2.2 TWh). At pjm-158's OWN measured channel gain (disarming moved CC_REGULAR +5.220/+6.848/+2.689 TWh against net positions +7.40/+6.48/-0.89, i.e. ~0.7-1.0 TWh CC per TWh net virtual) the held-out positions account for ~+6 and ~+10 TWh, or ~21 % of 2021's and ~44 % of 2022's CC_REGULAR miss (+28.7/+22.3 TWh classFull) — a BOUND transported across the tier boundary, NOT an attribution, and 55-79 % of the miss stays unexplained. NOT A LEVER: the root cause (the LP carries ONE price series, gated as RT, while the curve needs a DA price) remains the architecture question ESCALATED TO THE OWNER inside PJM's owner-declared-closed price-formation frontier (pjm-142); pjm-166 routes this as new evidence FOR that escalation and arms nothing. Also from the same phase 0, and it RETIRES the coal<->CC merit-order framing this cell has been read against: the gas/coal channel is ruled out three ways — in-sample elasticity already right (model 0.0686 vs actual 0.0772 on ln(delivered gas/coal), ratio 0.888, intercepts identical to 4 dp), coal NOT saturated (0.25-0.68 of its own annual peak in 2021's high-ratio months on a LARGER 2021 fleet, 36.9 vs 31.3 GW), and the SIGN TEST FAILS — 2021/2022 are the DEAREST-GAS and CHEAPEST-COAL years of the five on measured EIA-923 delivered receipts (gas 4.12/7.12 rank 4/5, coal 2.07/2.62 rank 1/2, vs gas 3.26/2.85 rank 2/1 in 2023/2024), so CC_REGULAR over-runs MOST where gas is DEAREST, the wrong sign for an offer-position error." },
