    rdt_tcdc: { cell: "." },
    seam_flow_envelopes: { cell: "K", ev: "pjm-95 (C1 interchange-duration root cause); pjm-151 (census registration + :7371 -> :9019 anchor repair; per-neighbour envelope PROMOTED, keeper 2026-08-03-pjm-151-seam-envelope, PREREG/FINDING-pjm151, gates results/calibration/_pjm151_seam_gates.json, ex ante measurement _pjm151_seam_envelope_attribution.json); pjm-153 — ROOT CAUSE (15-new) CLOSED BY MEASURED REFUTATION, no solve (FINDING-pjm153-queue-clear-2026-08-04.md §2; probe scripts/probes/pjm153_item15_ladder_attribution.py; machine record _pjm153_item15_attribution.json, over the committed pjm-152 Task-C scope file _pjm152_item15_scope.json). THREE results, and they retire item 15 rather than charter it. (1) THE 2025 'MODEL RUNS 5.21 TWh LONG' CLAUSE IS A BENCHMARK ARTIFACT: item 15 is stated against EIA-930 Total interchange, which in 2025 posts 17.968 TWh against PJM's settlement tie file at 32.925 and against EIA-930's OWN Net-generation-minus-Demand identity at 32.730 — it FAILS ITS OWN ARITHMETIC by 14.762 TWh with hourly r collapsing 0.976/0.9735 -> 0.3732. On the keeper's own attested net position (calibration_attestation free-parameter entry 14: 30.41/23.66/27.53 vs measured 39.98/32.83/32.93) the residual is ONE-SIGNED IN ALL THREE YEARS at -9.57/-9.17/-5.40 TWh: the model ALWAYS under-exports. (2) THE ENVELOPE CEILING CANNOT BIND — summing each seam's p90 export envelope over 8760 h gives 75.528/67.031/68.465 TWh against measured net export 39.975/32.824/32.925, i.e. 34-36 TWh of UNUSED HEADROOM every year, so loosening the caps or tuning PJM_TIE_NEIGHBOR / the p90 percentile would have been not merely barred (rules 5/14/20/24) but POINTLESS. (3) THE BINDING SIDE IS THE MODEL'S OWN PRICE DURATION CURVE. An export band clears when P(price <= p_k); the ladder's identification is EXACT (measured flow duration vs P(actual LMP <= p_k) agree to <= 0.0003 across all 40 bands, all three years), so evaluating the same band sum at the model's price is apples-to-apples: -8.290/-5.991/-4.152 TWh, i.e. 86.6/65.3/76.9 % of the shortfall. The deep bands never clear (MISO 2023 bands 6-8: measured 0.277/0.126/0.035 vs model 0.038/0.0006/0.000) because the model is TOO DEAR AT THE BOTTOM — p5 +$7.32/+$7.57/+$7.36 and p25 +$5.23/+$4.84/+$4.43 above actual, remarkably stable across years. THAT IS ITEMS 12-13, the flat-stack amplitude defect (+$6.82/+$5.78/+$3.40 too dear overnight), measured on the SEAM instead of on the clock. Item 15 therefore COLLAPSES INTO the already-diagnosed, owner-declared-frontier limitation and gets NO CHARTER OF ITS OWN — chartering it would re-open the frontier under a new name. STATED AGAINST INTEREST: the TWh figures are an ACCOUNTING attribution on the ladder's own bands, not an LP counterfactual — clearing those bands raises PJM's internal price (exports are load), which un-clears some, so the true equilibrium recovery is SMALLER; they bound direction and order of magnitude only. pjm-163 promotion re-stamp (2026-08-16, rule 28 / finding §4): keeper now 2026-08-15-pjm-162-inputclock — the input-clock repair moves the seam/diurnal evidence basis (fueltype series +1h in 2023/24; interchange envelopes and zonal shares move inside DST hours via the UTC-stamp read-site fix), so the p5/p25 dearness and band-clearing magnitudes above were measured at the PRE-repair inputs and stand as historical record; the K verdict (per-neighbour envelope, measured source unchanged) is NOT re-adjudicated" },
    miso_seam_envelope_hour_ending_key: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-only field (the seam-DIBA gate returns None for every other ISO — byte-identical; verified miso-175 V-3). Whether PJM's own seam-envelope analogue (pjm_seam_flow_limit — a DIFFERENT measured source, the PJM tie-line file, not the EIA-930 DIBA parquet) carries the same hour-key convention is PJM's lane's call, handed forward by FINDING-miso174 §4/§7 — not inspected or stamped by miso-175 (rule 25)." },
    m2m_seam_entitlement_cap: { cell: "U", ev: "UNTESTED and NOT a transfer (rules 25/28d): PJM is the other party to the SAME MISO-PJM JOA record (and posts its own M2M series via Data Miner); whether PJM's lane can use its side of the CMP record on its MISO seam is PJM's own call under its own charter and its own measured identification. MISO's G (miso-176) transfers nothing." },
    miso_seam_coincident_envelope: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-seam construction and refutation (the MISO-PJM EIA-930 DIBA seam conditioned on PJM's own load; miso-181). Rule 25: nothing transfers; a seam-response candidate in this ISO would be its own driver identification on its own seams." },
    miso_south_firm_export_block: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-South-seam construction and refusal (the EXPORT side of MISO's South DIBA pool - SOCO/TVA/AECI/LGEE/SIKE - on the Manitoba firm-block form; miso-182). Rule 25: nothing transfers. The binding objection is specific to MISO's non-contiguous footprint - its Midwest-to-South Regional Directional Transfer wheels across the same Joint-Party systems that constitute the seam - so no other ISO inherits either the candidate or the refusal." },
    miso_south_export_ladder_rt_tail: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-South-seam adjudication (the scarce-tail rebasis of MISO's own registered Q-Q seam ladder; miso-184). Rule 25: nothing transfers — the construction and its refusal live on MISO's measured seam record; a tail question on another ISO's ladder enters as its own adjudication on its own record." },
    miso_rdt_measured_limit: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-only adjudication (a measured hourly limit on MISO's Midwest↔South RDT contract-path corridor; miso-211). Rule 25: nothing transfers — no other ISO has the non-contiguous footprint, the published TCDC or the PBC binding record the construction and its refusal live on." },
    miso_south_gas_delivered_cost_basis: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-only adjudication (a South-zone-specific delivered gas cost basis for MISO's South gas fleet; miso-212). Rule 25: nothing transfers — the 923 prints, the zonal-basis leg and the RDT-binding hour set the decomposition lives on are MISO's own. The one cross-ISO item it surfaced — whether gas offers should carry the plant's EIA-923 AVERAGE delivered cost (the every-ISO convention) or marginal commodity — is owner-court and recorded on gas_hub_basis_overlay at MISO, not here." },
    miso_zonal_gas_basis_skip_923_priced: { cell: ".", ev: "MISO-only field (rule 25; miso-213). The same rule-19 layering exists in kind wherever the mean-zero core (basis/meanzero.py) runs under gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing — PJM's pjm_zonal_gas_basis included — but it enters this lane only as its own U candidate with its own population measurement, never from MISO's verdict." },
