    economic_retirement_screen: { cell: "R", fc: "R", ev: "ff-verdicts FC-3; FFR-2B (docs/handoffs/ffr-2b-retirement-entry-evidence-2026-08-02.md; runs pjm-2021-2025-cmc-{legacy,pipeline}-ffr2b); FFR-3A-2 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a2-battery-close-2026-08-03.md §3.8 — run pjm-2021-2025-ffr3a2, post-epoch + shipped posture: coal 0.0→18.309, gas_st 10.358→0.0, gas_ct 3.693→0.0, unit_recall_gt300 FAIL→PASS, retire.total 18.157→22.415 vs 11.121 actual — reproduces FFR-3C's membership-vs-calendar split in ONE leg); FFR-3A-3 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a3-battery-close-2026-08-04.md §2.4/§3 — run pjm-2021-2025-realized-ffr3a3 RE-MEASURES THAT SAME LEG at the post-FFR-3F HEAD 941f4983, which carries the UNCONDITIONAL G3 cap-grain fix 2adfb49 that the FFR-3A-2 numbers predate. coal economic 18.309→14.756 GW, retire.total_gw 22.415→18.862 vs 11.121 actual, recall PASS 13/17, false_retire still FAIL; gas_st/gas_ct 0.0 and announced nuclear 4.097 / biomass 0.009 unmoved, so the entire movement is confined to the coal channel. SUPERSEDES the FFR-3A-2 figures immediately above. The post-fix 14.756 GW is EXACTLY the value FFR-2B measured AGAINST A PAIRED CONTROL — recorded as CONVERGENCE, NOT ATTRIBUTION, because no control arm ran in FFR-3A-3 either. The FFR-3C membership-vs-calendar split SURVIVES (membership right, depth still 1.70x). CELL UNCHANGED and determination UNMOVED (HOLD): PJM OVER-retires, and the residual is the chartered G-31 lane's, not a tuning target) ALSO capx D58 (2026-09-06, FINDING-capx-d58-2026-09-06.md), the sector-gate leg's same-HEAD control e47fee08f5f37d6f: the 2022 screen fails 677 rows / 29,727.9 MW of which only 11.70 % (3,476.5 MW) is Sector 1 where MISO's is 76.8 %, and PJM's admission floor HAS headroom where MISO's has none (2022 admits 13,177.5 of 29,727.9 MW failing, 2023 admits 3,105.5 of 5,795.2). SURFACED THERE and routed as a rule-19 question: the screen's margins list DOUBLES as the D57 capacity sell-offer stack, so anything leaving the screen's candidate set also leaves the auction and becomes zero-priced price-taker supply (retirements.py:2856 / :2872 / :3199) - one filter doing two jobs, which the dated-plant exemption rides too." },
